---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets'
import scratch from '../images/scratch.jpg'
import webapp from '../images/webapp.jpg'
import pi from '../images/pi.jpg'
import Button from './Button.astro'
---

<section id="activities" class="p-6 flex flex-col items-center space-y-4">
  <h2>Activities</h2>
  <p class="pb-4">
    Here are a few examples of the sorts of things we do at CoderDojo.
  </p>
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-12 lg:grid-cols-3 text-justify px-4">
    <div class="flex flex-col space-y-4 items-center">
      <Image
        src={scratch}
        alt="Scratch Logo"
        class="w-48 lg:w-44 h-auto rounded-2xl"
      />
      <h3>Learn to code with Scratch</h3>
      <p>
        Scratch is a tool for building your own games and animated stories. The
        simple drag and drop interface makes it easy to bring ideas to life, and
        helps teach the building blocks of programming. See some of our Ninja's
        Scratch projects in our{' '}
        <a
          href="https://scratch.mit.edu/studios/32126251"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noreferrer"
        >
          Scratch Studio
        </a>
        .
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="flex flex-col space-y-4 items-center">
      <Image
        src={webapp}
        alt="A website viewed on a tablet"
        class="w-48 lg:w-44 h-auto rounded-2xl"
      />
      <h3>Build websites &amp; apps</h3>
      <p>
        When you're ready for something more advanced, try building your own
        website or app. This could be a game, something more practical, or
        anything you can imagine!
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="flex flex-col space-y-4 items-center">
      <Image
        src={pi}
        alt="A Raspberry Pi circuit board"
        class="w-48 lg:w-44 h-auto rounded-2xl"
      />
      <h3>Hardware &amp; Robotics</h3>
      <p>
        In future Dojo sessions, we will look at using code outside of our
        laptops, to create things like robots and musical instruments.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="pt-6">
    If you'd like to see the sorts of things we build (or if you'd like to give
    them a try outside of the Dojo) click this button to find instructions for
    hundreds of examples!
  </p>
  <Button href="https://projects.raspberrypi.org/en/projects" external>
    CoderDojo Projects
  </Button>
</section>
